CASE = [
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> A class visited a garden in Jaipur and listed these plants: tulsi, rose, mango, pumpkin and grapevine. The teacher said plants can be grouped as herbs, shrubs, trees, creepers and climbers by the nature of their stems. "
   "(i) Name the plant from the list that is a tree. (ii) Which plant is a creeper? (iii) Give one difference between a herb and a shrub. (iv) How is a climber different from a creeper? Give an example of a climber from the list.",
   "(i) Mango (1). (ii) Pumpkin (1). (iii) Herb: small with soft, green stem; shrub: bushy with a hard stem branching near the base (1). (iv) A creeper spreads on the ground with a weak stem (1); a climber climbs up a support with tendrils or other parts; example: grapevine (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> Farhan pulled out a wheat seedling and a mustard seedling from his field. The wheat had many thin roots of equal size spreading from the stem base and its leaf had parallel veins. The mustard had one thick main root with thinner side branches and its leaf had a net of veins. "
   "(i) What type of roots does wheat have? (ii) Which plant has a tap root? (iii) What is the arrangement of veins in a leaf called? (iv) Name the venation of the mustard leaf and name one more plant with a tap root.",
   "(i) Fibrous roots (1). (ii) Mustard (1). (iii) Venation (1). (iv) Reticulate venation (1); carrot (or mango, gram) (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> Camels live in the Thar desert, where it is very hot and water is scarce. They have long legs, broad padded feet and thick eyelashes, and can go for many days without drinking water. Fish in a river, on the other hand, have gills and fins. "
   "(i) What is the place where an organism lives called? (ii) Name one feature of a camel that helps it walk on sand. (iii) Which body part helps a fish to breathe in water? (iv) What is meant by adaptation? Why is a camel not suited to live in a river?",
   "(i) Habitat (1). (ii) Broad padded feet (1). (iii) Gills (1). (iv) Adaptation is a feature that helps an organism live in its habitat (1); a camel has no gills or fins, so it cannot breathe or swim in water (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
]

